For a real ordinate $t$, combining the reciprocals of $1/2+it$ and $1/2-it$ gives $1/(1/4+t^2)$. Every denominator is positive. Therefore each new pair adds a positive term, and every finite nonempty window has positive total harmonic.
</details>

